.TH NAUTILUS-KDECONNECT 1 "October 2026" "scripts" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
nautilus-kdeconnect \- compatibility bridge translating kdeconnect:// URLs and recovering zombie FUSE mounts for GNOME Nautilus
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nautilus-kdeconnect
[\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR]
[\fB\-r\fR|\fB\-\-reset\fR [\fIDEVICE_ID\fR]]
[\fIURI\fR|\fIPATH\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBnautilus-kdeconnect\fR is a desktop compatibility bridge and protocol handler designed to allow GNOME \fBNautilus\fR to seamlessly browse file systems exposed by \fBKDE Connect\fR.
.PP
By default, KDE Connect dispatches file manager requests using KDE-native KIO URLs (such as \fBkdeconnect://<device-id>\fR) or temporary KIOExec wrapper cache directories (\fB~/.cache/kioexec/krun/...\fR). GNOME Nautilus does not implement the KIO subsystem, causing browsing actions to fail or open invalid temporary directories.
.PP
Furthermore, when Android devices enter deep sleep (Doze mode) or roam between Wi-Fi networks, FUSE mounts frequently degrade into "zombie" states (\fBd---------\fR, \fBInput/output error (os error 5)\fR), causing Nautilus to hang indefinitely. \fBnautilus-kdeconnect\fR automatically detects hanging or dead mounts, executes non-blocking lazy unmounting (\fBfusermount3 -u -z\fR), clears orphan \fBsshfs\fR processes, and re-triggers mounting via \fBkdeconnect-cli\fR before forwarding sanitized paths to the native \fBnautilus\fR binary.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-reset " [" \fIDEVICE_ID\fR "]"
Performs emergency recovery and remounting of hanging or zombie FUSE mounts. If \fIDEVICE_ID\fR is specified, resets that device's mount. If omitted, scans all active mounts under \fB/run/user/$UID\fR.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Displays brief command-line synopsis and exits.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Open device storage directly by device ID:
.RS
.nf
nautilus-kdeconnect kdeconnect://123456789abcdef
.fi
.RE
.PP
Perform an emergency reset of all hanging KDE Connect mounts:
.RS
.nf
nautilus-kdeconnect --reset
.fi
.RE
.PP
Reset and remount a specific phone device:
.RS
.nf
nautilus-kdeconnect --reset 0ea371db39424699b44e8f13a548be3b
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR nautilus (1),
.BR sshfs (1),
.BR kdeconnect-cli (1),
.BR scripts (1)
